orting adoption statistics (60% of healthcare systems implementing)\",\n    45→    \"emotionalArc\": \"Promise → Evidence → Doubt → Resolution (hope through collaboration)\"\n    46→  },\n    47→  \"coreIdeas\": [\n    48→    \"Diagnostic Acceleration - AI detects diseases faster and with higher accuracy than humans\",\n    49→    \"Drug Development Efficiency - ML reduces development time and dramatically lowers costs\",\n    50→    \"Personalized Treatment - AI customizes medicine based on individual genetic and lifestyle data\",\n    51→    \"Human-AI Collaboration - Future is augmentation and partnership, not replacement\",\n    52→    \"Market Adoption - Healthcare organizations actively investing in AI infrastructure\",\n    53→    \"Preventive Medicine - AI enables prediction and prevention before disease manifests\",\n    54→    \"Systemic Transformation - AI reshapes workflows and professional roles across healthcare\"\n    55→  ],\n    56→  \"importantQuotes\": [\n    57→    {\n    58→      \"text\": \"Artificial intelligence is fundamentally transforming the healthcare industry. From diagnostic imaging to personalized medicine, AI systems are becoming integral to modern medical practice.\",\n    59→      \"context\": \"Opening paragraph establishing the central premise and scope of the article\",\n    60→      \"significance\": \"Sets the foundational claim for all subsequent discussion\"\n    61→    },\n    62→    {\n    63→      \"text\": \"Machine learning models trained on millions of medical images have achieved accuracy rates exceeding 95% in detecting breast cancer, lung cancer, and other conditions.\",\n    64→      \"context\": \"Within Diagnostic Revolution section, providing specific quantifiable evidence of AI capability\",\n    65→      \"significance\": \"Establishes concrete, credible evidence of AI's diagnostic superiority\"\n    66→    },\n    67→    {\n    68→      \"text\": \"What might take a radiologist 15 minutes to analyze, an AI sy